<tr><td colspan=4><font size=2 face=verdana color=#ffffff>I am in the Army, and as of now, I am currently in the field alot, so That is why I am not on as much as I'd like to be.  I get on every chance I get, and every time there are new members that I haven't met, so if you don't know me, I'd love to meet you, and battle alongside ya!  FOR KALADIM!!!!!!

Now, for some background on myself...   
     Lowbeard was born of a proud family of bearded dwarves.  The longest beard in his family, surprisingly enough, was that of his mother.  Her beard always mad his father jealous.  In Lowbeards younger days, he spent his time keeping away from all the violence around him.  He hoped he would never have to deal with the problems of the outside world.  He preferred the idea of educating himself.  Trying very hard to learn as many languages as possible, he studied for many moons.  This was not easy for Lowbeard, for he was not the brightest dwarf in the bundle, but his will to learn was enough to drive him to success.  
     One beautiful morning, Lowbeard was returning home from a walk to the Paladin's guild in Kaladim, where he had hoped to find a book or something to help him finish learning the language of Dragons.  Upon entering his parents stone built home, he found that the ground was covered in blood.  His parents had been brutally murdered.  His father's torso lie on the ground, ripped from the rest of his body, and all that was left of his mother was her head, and some entrails.  Enraged, lowbeard felt his blood boil.  Grabbing his father's sword from the storage box under the bed, and grabbing his baby brother, Darkbeard, he fled the home, and handed over custody of Darkbeard to the warriors guild in Kaladim.  They took pity on Lowbeard, and Gave him some patchwork armor.  They told him that they would care for Darkbeard, if Lowbeard would commit to service for the guild.  Lowbeard smiled, and gladly accepted the deal.  
     Training with the sword, he ravashed through the monsters of the Butcherblock mountains.  Unsure of who or what had killed his parents, he vowed to destroy every hostile creature in his path until he found his answer.  During his search, Lowbeard had learned that the attack on his parents was probably made by the ogres of ButcherBlock.  Without hessitation, Lowbeard grabbed his blade and dashed towards the mountains.  First he spotted the male ogre, Cornfluk.  Cornfluk was an easy kill for Lowbeard, sneaking up behind him and slitting his throat before the foul ogre even knew what was coming.  A few days later, Lowbeard had awakened to the sound of heavy footsteps.  He could smell an ogre a mile away, and knew that it must be the counterpart of Cornfluk, Zarchoomi.  Rushing towards the female beast, his eyes burned red.  But to Lowbeards surprise, he was struck by a burst of force that came out of nowhere.  It appeared taht this ogre was more that met the eye.  He slashed at the hideous ogre with all his might, and Zarchoomi pounded Lowbeard with everything she had.  Lowbeard had been injured badly, and would surely die soon if he did not run, but suddenly, he felt a healing touch.  He immidiatley used all of his strength to slice down Zarchoomi once and for all.   After tha attel was over, Lowbeard turned around to see a tall half elf standing behind him.  With a sword and shield in hand, the half-elf bowed.  "thank you sir", said Lowbeard. 
     "No need for thanks.  The name's Bindail" spoke the Paladin.  THey had soon become very good friends, and went on many adventures together.  One day while hunting for alligator skins in the oasis of Marr, they came across a beautiful wood elf named Daphnei.  Finding her to be a good friend, and powerfull ally, they decided to join her group, the Norrath Militia.  The rest as you know, is History...&nbsp;</font></td></tr>

